  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1107.02 Off-site Shipments",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1107.02 Off-site Shipments.\n\n(a) An owner or operator of a destination facility shall not send or take universal waste to a place other than a universal waste handler, another destination facility, or a foreign destination.\n\n(b) An owner or operator of a destination facility that rejects a shipment or a portion of a shipment shall notify the universal waste handler that originated the shipment that the shipment has been rejected, and either:\n\n(1) Send the shipment back to the universal waste handler that originated the shipment; or\n\n(2) Send the shipment to another destination facility designated by the universal waste handler that originated the shipment.\n\n(c) If an owner or operator of a destination facility receives a shipment containing hazardous waste that is not a universal waste, the owner or operator of the destination facility shall:\n\n(1) Immediately notify the department of the shipment;\n\n(2) Provide the name, address, and phone number of the shipper; and\n\n(3) Comply with the applicable requirements of Env-Hw 400 through Env-Hw 800 and Env-Hw 1200 for managing the hazardous waste.\n\nSource. #7578, eff 10-13-01; (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Hw 1100) ss by #9367, eff 1-28-09; ss by #12353, eff 8-14-17; ss by #13406, eff 7-23-22; ss by #14281, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1100.html"
